From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:03:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 012/191] [ae-patch] Show a merge card per tracked pull request
 in the GitHub panel and the chat

Reid merges from his phone and had to leave OmniGent for github.com to do it.
The session's GitHub panel now opens with a card per pull request the session
tracks (upstream's per-session tracking, the panel's own prs list): title and
link, repo and head branch, CI with counts, mergeability, review state, and a
Merge button. The same card, compact, sits under an assistant message that
names one of the session's tracked pull requests, so a PR the agent just
opened can be merged where it was announced.

The cards read omnigent-ae's GET /v1/ae/prs/{owner}/{repo}/{n}, which decides
whether Merge is live and why not (CI failing or running, conflicted, blocked
or behind, draft, changes requested), so every card agrees with the
Dashboard's Open PRs card. Merge asks once (squash or merge commit, the repo's
allowed methods, squash first), then posts the head SHA the card showed to
POST .../merge; a refusal shows the reason and the fresh card. After a merge
the card shows the result and offers "Set this session to review" through the
labels PATCH the Status submenu already uses. Targets are 44 px below md.

The inline card reads the tracked list from the panel's cached query and
never fetches it; while that list is unknown (runner asleep) any readable
pull request URL in the message gets a card, and one the token cannot read
shows nothing.

New files lib/aePrs.ts, components/AePrCards.tsx and
components/AeInlinePrCards.tsx; two lines in shell/GithubPanel.tsx and two in
components/blocks/BlockRenderer.tsx (the import and the element each).

